{"id":"nchi-0b5987","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"New chat in an untrusted folder: first message is lost behind Claude's trust question","description":"**Found in nchi-020665, check 8.** Sending a new chat with ~/Downloads as the folder showed \"couldn't start\" in Nocchi. Herdr's pane showed Claude's \"Accessing workspace… Is this a project you created or one you trust?\" question.\n\n**Cause:** `HerdrAdapter` starts the agent, then sends the message with `agent.prompt`. In a folder Claude hasn't trusted yet, Claude asks first, so the agent is waiting for you (log: `wX:p1 idle → blocked` three seconds after it appeared). The prompt isn't accepted, the 15 s retry window runs out, and Nocchi reports the failure. The agent keeps running without the message.\n\n**Fix:** pass the message at launch instead. Herdr's `AgentStartParams` has `args: [String]`, which runs `claude \"\u003cmessage\u003e\"`. Claude holds the message through the trust question and starts on it once you answer; Nocchi meanwhile shows the agent as needing you. Drop the separate `agent.prompt`. For kinds whose CLI doesn't take a prompt argument, keep the prompt-after-start path.\n\n**Check:** `HerdrRequest.startAgent` with `args` passes the installed Herdr's schema (SchemaDrift test). An integration test in an isolated Herdr session can check the argv Herdr reports back (`agent_started` includes `argv`) without sending anything to Claude.","sort_order":"aJ","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-0b5987","target_id":"nchi-020665","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","herdr"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:50:54.635792Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-448189","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Clicking outside the open chat closes in two steps (chat shrinks, then the notch collapses)","description":"**Found in nchi-020665, check 2.** Clicking outside the notch while the chat field is open plays two animations: first the composer shrinks back into the cards, then about 350 ms later the notch collapses.\n\n**Cause:** the panel losing focus sets `prompt = .none`, and the overview animates the composer back to the focus card. `promptChanged(.none)` then calls `scheduleModeChange()`, which collapses after `collapseDelay` because the pointer is outside.\n\n**Fix:** when the field closes because of a click elsewhere and the pointer is outside the notch, collapse right away so the composer leaves with the notch, in a single motion. Closing with Home or Esc while the pointer is over the notch keeps today's shrink-back animation.","sort_order":"aK","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-448189","target_id":"nchi-020665","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:50:54.655119Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-020665","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2734be56-e3a5-417c-928a-91584cc33db6","text":"Checked on screen with the user (2026-10-02):\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 1 Tabs, 3 folder menu, 4 Choose…, 5 gear, 6 source badges | OK |\n| 2 Draft survives | OK, but closing animates in two steps → `nchi-448189` |\n| 7 External display | OK (\"look amazing\") |\n| 8 Send through Herdr | Failed in an untrusted folder (~/Downloads): Claude's trust question blocks the first message → `nchi-0b5987` |\n| 9 Terminal fallback | Not tested. The user would rather the fallback owner be the Claude Desktop app, then a Nocchi-owned subprocess, instead of a terminal tab; to be designed as its own issue |\n\nNo code changes in this issue."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:51:03.848269Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-d952cb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"New agent typed into a shell still starting up: \"claude\" becomes \"laude\"","description":"**Found in nchi-020665, check 8**, in a folder Claude already trusts (/Users/me/Scratch). The new Herdr pane showed oh-my-zsh's \"Would you like to update? [Y/n]\", which read the `c` of `claude` as its answer. The shell then ran `laude`: \"command not found\".\n\n**Cause:** `agent.start` types the agent command into the pane's shell. Herdr treats the pane as ready although the shell is still running its startup files and reading from the keyboard. Any startup question (oh-my-zsh updates, direnv, a `read` in .zshrc) swallows part of the command.\n\n**Fix direction:** don't type into a shell. Create the pane with the agent as its process: `layout.apply` with a pane node `{cwd, command: [\"claude\", \"\u003cmessage\u003e\"]}`. That also passes the first message at launch, which fixes nchi-0b5987. To check in an isolated Herdr session:\n- `PATH` in that process (is `claude` found?)\n- Herdr still detects the agent\n- what happens to the pane when the agent exits","sort_order":"aL","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-d952cb","target_id":"nchi-020665","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"nchi-d952cb","target_id":"nchi-0b5987","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","herdr"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:52:38.553023Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-6b5dc7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"New chat fails with agent_name_taken when the folder already has a Herdr agent","description":"**Found in nchi-020665, check 8.** With a Herdr workspace already open in /Users/me/Scratch (empty terminal), sending a new chat for that folder failed: \"Herdr error agent_name_taken: agent name scratch is already used\".\n\n**Cause:** `HerdrAdapter.start` names every agent after its folder (`agentName(label)`), and Herdr's `agent.start` requires unique names. It also always creates a new workspace, even when one is already open in that folder.\n\n**Expected:** reuse the workspace already open in that folder and start the agent in a new tab there. Otherwise create a workspace.\n\n**Fix:** part of nchi-d952cb's change. Starting through `layout.apply` (a pane whose process is the agent) needs no agent name, and given an existing workspace's ID it adds a new tab.","sort_order":"aM","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-6b5dc7","target_id":"nchi-020665","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"nchi-6b5dc7","target_id":"nchi-d952cb","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","herdr"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:54:09.595895Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
