{"id":"nchi-d952cb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-111441cc-4a1e-44d3-88a9-9b843f2a1970","text":"Implemented per spec (with the user's decisions: the pane closes when the agent exits; always a new tab; the tab is named after the message). Not committed yet; the branch build is running for the user to try.\n\n- `HerdrAdapter.start`:\n  - finds the folder's workspace via `pane.list` (`cwd` or `foreground_cwd`, symlinks resolved, so `/tmp` matches `/private/tmp`)\n  - otherwise `workspace.create`, then `layout.apply` with `command: [agent, message]` and `tab_label`\n  - closes the new workspace's shell pane afterwards (or on failure)\n  - `agent.prompt` after start only for kinds other than claude and codex\n- Removed `agent.start`, `HerdrRequest.startAgent`, `agentName` and their test. `herdrKind` is now `HerdrAdapter.command(for:)`, injectable through `init(agentCommand:)`.\n- New requests `listPanes` and `applyLayout`, both in `HerdrRequest.all` for the schema drift test.\n- Tests:\n  - `tabsAreNamedAfterTheMessage`\n  - integration `startsAgentsInTheirFoldersWorkspace`, with a fake agent script and no real agent: covers reuse vs create, two starts in one folder (no name clash), tab names, and the message argv arriving exactly, quotes and `$HOME` intact\n- PLAN.md: the M5 notes describe the new start path; \"No resends\" names `layout.apply` and `workspace.create`.\n- `swift test`: 138 passed. No `nocchi-it-*` sessions left over.\n\nNot in the spec: the tab label is cut at 24 characters on a word boundary, and an over-long single word is cut hard at 23 characters plus \"…\"."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:59:26.636125Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-2b1824","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Messaging an agent: short folder label in the composer's folder chip","description":"The composer for an existing (idle) agent shows the full path (\"/Users/me/code/acme/nocchi\"). The new-chat folder button already shortens it (\"acme/nocchi\", nchi-… commit `c0957e8`).\n\nUse the same label in `ContextChip`, with the full path in the tooltip. Move the label logic out of `FolderPicker` into one shared helper, so both chips use it.\n\nRequested by the user, 2026-10-02.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","labels":["task","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T08:02:37.319866Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
