{"id":"nchi-acbee0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Claude sessions spawned by a non-agent process in a Herdr pane are invisible","description":"A Claude session that a non-agent process starts inside a Herdr pane (e.g. `xpo board`'s agent chat, through the Agent SDK) doesn't show up in Nocchi.\n\n## Cause\n- The registry entry is `\"kind\":\"interactive\"`, `\"entrypoint\":\"sdk-cli\"`, so `ClaudeRegistry` keeps it.\n- Process chain: `claude → xpo → -zsh → herdr`. This was confirmed live on 2026-10-15 for 3 `xpo`-spawned sessions.\n- `ProcessContext` in `ClaudeAdapter.swift` sets `insideHerdr` when *any* ancestor is `herdr`. `ClaudeSessionTracker.applyRegistry` then skips the session and leaves it to HerdrAdapter.\n- Herdr doesn't list the pane in `agents[]`, because its process is `xpo`, not an agent. So neither adapter shows the session.\n\n## Expected\nA session is left to Herdr only when Herdr reports it as the pane's agent. Otherwise ClaudeAdapter shows it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] An SDK-spawned `claude` under a non-agent process in a Herdr pane appears through ClaudeAdapter.\n- [ ] A `claude` run directly in a Herdr pane still appears exactly once (through HerdrAdapter).\n- [ ] Tests cover both process chains.","sort_order":"aJ","labels":["bug","herdr"]},"created_at":"2026-10-15T21:49:47.556425Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-acbee0","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-10-15T21:49:57.233909Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.299 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
