{"id":"nchi-09c34c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Claude agent stays \"working\" after its turn ends while a background command runs","description":"Reported live: Servaint (Claude Code 2.1.301 in Ghostty) shows working, but its turn finished.\n\nRoot cause: Claude's session registry reported `busy → shell` at the exact moment the turn ended (statusUpdatedAt 12:51:56Z = the transcript's `turn_duration` line). The session had started `make dev` as a background command, which is still running. So `shell` means \"idle, with a background command still running\", not \"running a command in this turn\": while a foreground Bash call runs, the status stays `busy` (checked on a live session). `ClaudeSessionTracker.status` maps `shell` → working, so the agent stays working for as long as the dev server lives.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-09c34c","target_id":"nchi-d320c5","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-16T12:57:44.280475Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.301 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
