{"id":"nchi-169460","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Herdr GUI adapter: agents from herdr-core (hc), window actions through herdr-app","description":"Herdr moved from the TUI (`herdr`, protocol 22) to a GUI split into two independent pieces: **herdr-core** (`hc`, terminals + agent status, JSON-RPC 2.0 on `~/.local/state/herdr-core/default/default.sock`) and **herdr-app** (the window: spaces/tabs/panes, control socket `~/.config/herdr-app/herdr-app.sock`).\n\nAdd a new adapter for them, alongside the existing TUI `HerdrAdapter`:\n- Agents and status from `hc` `events.subscribe` (snapshot + ordered events + heartbeat + `missed`).\n- prompt → `terminal.send`; focus/open → herdr-app `agent.focus` + raise Herdr.app; start → herdr-app `tab.new`/`space.new` with `argv` + `task`.\n- Settings: new \"Herdr\" source (default on); the old one becomes \"Herdr (TUI)\".\n- ClaudeAdapter leaves sessions inside hc terminals to the new adapter when it's on (no duplicates).\n- Schema drift test against `hc schema`.\n\nOut of scope for v1: remote machines (`hc machine`).","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-169460","target_id":"nchi-acbee0","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","herdr"]},"created_at":"2026-11-09T14:36:02.317608Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.319 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
