{"id":"nchi-169460","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6f37a281-62d0-41ff-850a-033727c0d7ee","text":"Implementation ready for review (branch `nchi-169460-herdr-gui-adapter-agents-from-herdr-core-hc`).\n\n- New target `NocchiHerdrCore`: `HcClient` (JSON-RPC, per-request connections + a dedicated subscription), `HerdrAppClient` (window control socket), `HcTracker` (pure), `HerdrCoreAdapter` (id `hc`). Reuses `HerdrConnection` (now `package`).\n- Settings: \"Herdr\" (`usesHerdrCore`, default on) + \"Herdr (TUI)\" (`usesHerdr`, now default off when never set). Overview shows both. `make live` defaults to hc (`SOURCE=herdr-tui|claude`).\n- ClaudeAdapter leaves sessions under `herdr-core` to the hc adapter when it's on.\n- Off-spec additions: Claude session ID from `~/.claude/sessions/\u003cpid\u003e.json` so steps/messages work; `isFocused` not set in v1; status/turn ordering handled in the tracker.\n- Tests: 13 new (tracker fixtures from a real core, contract + integration against an isolated core, schema drift vs `hc schema`). Full suite 163/163. One unrelated flake seen once in the TUI `focusAndUnknownAgents` test under parallel load; passed 3/3 on rerun.\n- Live: `make live` shows `hc/t11 Claude working \"Open-Source\"` with steps and the latest message.\n- Not yet verified on the real window: focus/open and start (they change the user's screen)."},"created_at":"2026-11-09T14:47:45.609395Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.319 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
