{"id":"nchi-9e4c20","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Choose which agent new chats start and where they land","description":"Today Chat and folder drops always start Claude (`.start(kind: .claude, …)` is hard-coded in `NotchModel`/`NotchController`), and the store picks the destination automatically (`AgentStore.starter`: connected, then can-prompt, then **adapter id alphabetically**, so `hc` beats `herdr` only by name).\n\nProposal:\n- **Agent picker** in the Chat tab next to the folder picker: Claude, Codex, pi, OpenCode, Copilot. It remembers the last choice, and folder drops use it too.\n- **\"New agents start in\"** setting: Automatic / Herdr / Herdr (TUI) / Terminal tab. Automatic should prefer Herdr (hc) over the TUI on purpose, not by sort order.\n- Not in scope: providers' native apps (Claude desktop, Codex app). Nocchi can launch them but can't watch them or send them messages.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aJ","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-9e4c20","target_id":"nchi-169460","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-11-09T15:50:43.47517Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.319 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-3350b0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Drop files, images and URLs on the notch","description":"Today only folders can be dropped, and a folder starts a new agent there.\n\nProposal:\n- **On an agent's face or chip** (adapters with `.prompt`): a file path or URL is sent to that agent as a message. An image goes through hc `terminal.put` (it lands beside the agent's terminal and its path is pasted in), for agents in the Herdr app.\n- **On the empty notch:** open Chat with a draft such as \"Look at `\u003cfile\u003e`\" in the file's folder (or its repo root), or with the URL filled in. Don't send automatically, so the user can edit first.\n- Anything other than a folder always drafts rather than sending right away: a mis-dropped file shouldn't start a turn.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aK","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-3350b0","target_id":"nchi-169460","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-11-09T15:50:43.501438Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.319 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-7f44f6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"README: document the Herdr app source (herdr-core + herdr-app)","description":"Follow-up to nchi-169460. The README only describes the Herdr TUI.\n\n- [ ] Intro/Requirements: the Herdr app (hc 0.1.x + herdr-app) as the main Herdr source, TUI optional\n- [ ] Features: click-to-write and folder drop work through the Herdr app (space or tab)\n- [ ] Settings: Sources = Herdr, Herdr (TUI), Claude Code; `herdrSession`/`herdrSocketPath` are TUI-only\n- [ ] Development: `make test` runs herdr-core integration tests when `hc` is installed; `make live SOURCE=herdr-tui|claude`\n- [ ] Library products: add `NocchiHerdrCore`","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@mbpm1x.local\u003e","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-7f44f6","target_id":"nchi-169460","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-11-09T15:52:53.944201Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.319 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
