{"id":"nchi-7e6772","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Update-available notification based on new commits on GitHub main","description":"Nocchi has no prebuilt releases — users build from source (`make install`). There's no way for a running copy to know it's behind. Add an \"update available\" notification driven by commits on `nicbet/nocchi` main.\n\n## Sketch\n- **Embed the build commit:** `scripts/bundle.sh` currently only writes the version from `Nocchi.swift` into Info.plist. Also record the git SHA it was built from (e.g. a custom `NocchiGitCommit` Info.plist key), plus whether the tree was dirty or off main.\n- **Check GitHub:** periodically (e.g. on launch + every few hours) hit the public API, `GET /repos/nicbet/nocchi/commits/main`, and compare its SHA to the embedded one. Use `compare/{built}...main` to get \"N commits behind\" and recent commit subjects if useful. Unauthenticated; respect rate limits and ETag/`If-None-Match`.\n- **Notify:** show an unobtrusive \"update available\" state in the notch/menu (and/or a user notification), with the update instructions (`git pull \u0026\u0026 make install`) or a link to the commits.\n- **Settings:** a toggle to turn update checks off; no network calls when disabled.\n\n## Open questions\n- Notch indicator, macOS notification, menu item, or a mix?\n- Notify on any commit to main, or only when the `version` string changes?\n- Builds from a fork, local branch, or dirty tree: skip the check, or compare against upstream anyway?\n- Offer a one-click \"pull and rebuild\", or just tell the user how?\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Built app knows the commit SHA it was built from\n- [ ] Running app detects when GitHub main has moved past that commit\n- [ ] User sees a non-intrusive update-available indication with how to update\n- [ ] Checks can be disabled and fail silently when offline/rate-limited","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"aL","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-09T15:59:31.397711Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.319 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-a4f8e6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Nocchi bots: persistent, headless agent identities owned by Nocchi","description":"Persistent bots owned by Nocchi, so adding one no longer opens a Herdr space, tab or window. A bot is an **identity** stored on disk: a name, a harness (Claude Code or Codex), a model, a persona, a folder and a face. It runs as a **headless** harness process that Nocchi starts and supervises. Bots are restored when Nocchi launches and keep their conversation across restarts.\n\nDecisions so far (from discussion with the developer, 2026-11-13):\n- Headless only. No \"open in terminal\" escape hatch: Nocchi is the only UI for a bot.\n- The new-bot form picks the harness and model and gives the bot an identity.\n- Bots can do anything on the computer: no permission prompts, no sandbox. That includes computer use.\n- Neither CLI gives a headless bot computer use. Claude Code's computer use doesn't work with `-p`, and Codex's is a feature of the Codex desktop app only. So Nocchi provides it through its own MCP server, which it gives every bot.\n\nChildren:\n1. Bot identity store and lazy restore\n2. Headless runtimes (Claude stream-json, Codex app-server) behind a `bots` adapter\n3. Nocchi MCP server: computer use, screen lock, ask_user, set_mood\n4. Bot UI: new-bot form, writing to a bot, transcript view","sort_order":"aM","labels":["epic"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:22:51.733382Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-99df2d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Bot identity store: ~/.config/nocchi/bots, separate state, lazy restore as asleep faces","description":"A bot's identity lives in a file you can edit by hand, one per bot: `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nocchi/bots/\u003cslug\u003e.toml`, defaulting to `~/.config`. Changing runtime state (session or thread ID, last activity) is kept separately in `~/Library/Application Support/Nocchi/bots/\u003cslug\u003e.json`. On launch every bot appears as an asleep face, with no process running. The directory is watched, so adding, editing or deleting a file updates the bots live.","parent_id":"nchi-a4f8e6","sort_order":"aN","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:23:03.081739Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-ae71db","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Headless bot runtimes: Claude stream-json and Codex app-server behind a `bots` adapter","description":"A new `NocchiBots` module and `bots` adapter. Each bot is a supervised child process. For Claude: `claude -p --input-format stream-json --output-format stream-json --verbose --permission-mode bypassPermissions --model \u003cm\u003e --append-system-prompt \u003cpersona\u003e --session-id|--resume \u003cid\u003e --mcp-config \u003cnocchi\u003e`. For Codex: `codex app-server` over JSON-RPC stdio (`thread/start` / `thread/resume`, `turn/start`), with approvals off and full access. The adapter maps the harness events onto AgentStatus, steps and titles. A message to an asleep bot wakes it. Bots go back to sleep after an idle timeout.","parent_id":"nchi-a4f8e6","sort_order":"aO","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:23:03.11146Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-5a9c2c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Nocchi MCP server: computer use, single screen lock, ask_user, set_mood","description":"Nocchi runs its own MCP server and gives it to every bot. Computer-use tools: screenshot, click, type, key, scroll, open_app, list_windows. These use Nocchi's own Accessibility and Screen Recording permissions. Only one bot may drive the screen at a time, and the notch shows which face is driving. Esc or a click on the notch takes control back. Nocchi-specific tools: `ask_user`, which shows a question in the notch and puts the bot in the blocked/needs-you state, and `set_mood`. This is needed because neither harness gives a headless bot computer use.","parent_id":"nchi-a4f8e6","sort_order":"aP","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:23:03.144978Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-58bfcf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Bot UI: new-bot form (harness, model, identity), write to a bot, transcript view","description":"A new-bot form in the expanded notch: name, harness (Claude or Codex), model, persona, folder, face tint. It writes the identity file. A bot's chip and face take messages through the existing composer. With no terminal, each bot needs a scrollable transcript view (its messages, tool steps and answers), reached from its chip or face. Answering `ask_user` questions also happens here.","parent_id":"nchi-a4f8e6","sort_order":"aQ","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:23:03.174804Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
