{"id":"nchi-5dc8bf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"User-defined MCP servers for bots: ~/.config/nocchi/mcp.toml, per-bot opt-in, strict","description":"You define MCP servers once in `~/.config/nocchi/mcp.toml`, and each bot opts into the ones it needs with `mcp = [...]` in its identity file. When a bot wakes, Nocchi writes that harness's MCP config (pass-through), and the harness starts the servers itself. Strict: a bot gets only the servers Nocchi defines plus the built-in `nocchi` server, never your global Claude or Codex servers. An import action copies servers in from `~/.claude.json` and `~/.codex/config.toml`. Secrets are referenced from Keychain. A gateway that proxies the servers (option 2) is deliberately left for later; the config is shaped so it can be added without changing any files.","parent_id":"nchi-a4f8e6","sort_order":"aR","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-5dc8bf","target_id":"nchi-99df2d","kind":"depends_on"},{"source_id":"nchi-5dc8bf","target_id":"nchi-ae71db","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"nchi-5dc8bf","target_id":"nchi-58bfcf","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:45:29.691066Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-5dc8bf","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:45:51.692588Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-a4f8e6","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-11-13T09:46:02.77866Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-c72bcc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Bot computers: a Linux VM per bot (base image, COW clones, suspend/resume, viewer)","description":"Each bot gets its own computer: a Linux VM run by Nocchi through Apple's Virtualization.framework. VMs are copy-on-write clones of one base image, run only while the bot is awake, and are suspended when it sleeps. The bot's harness runs inside the VM, and the bot's folder is shared into the VM. The VM's screen can be watched and taken over in Nocchi. Set with `computer = \"own\"` (the default), `\"\u003cname\u003e\"` for a VM shared by bots that name it, or `\"host\"` to drive your Mac (explicit opt-in).","parent_id":"nchi-a4f8e6","sort_order":"aS","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-c72bcc","target_id":"nchi-99df2d","kind":"depends_on"},{"source_id":"nchi-c72bcc","target_id":"nchi-ae71db","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"nchi-c72bcc","target_id":"nchi-5a9c2c","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"nchi-c72bcc","target_id":"nchi-58bfcf","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"nchi-c72bcc","target_id":"nchi-5dc8bf","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T10:31:51.119181Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-42b3e7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Bot computers v2: macOS VMs (computer = { kind = \"macos\" })","description":"For bots that need Mac apps, a v2 option to make a bot's computer a macOS VM (Virtualization.framework, built from an IPSW restore image), next to the v1 Linux VM. Limits to design around: Apple's licence allows at most 2 extra macOS VMs per Mac, each image is tens of GB, each running VM takes several GB of RAM, and signing in to an Apple ID inside a VM is awkward. Probably shared named computers rather than one per bot. Plan this after nchi-c72bcc ships.","parent_id":"nchi-a4f8e6","sort_order":"aT","dependencies":[{"source_id":"nchi-42b3e7","target_id":"nchi-c72bcc","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-11-13T10:31:54.8454Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.323 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
